extensions. Counts are parameter points, not independent index builds.}
\label{tab:b-e1-counts}
\footnotesize\setlength{\tabcolsep}{4pt}
\input{tables/appendix/e1-counts}
\end{minipage}\par\medskip

\begingroup\raggedright
\paragraph{JHQ-GPU.}
All E1 points use $B=B_r=8$, $M=d/8$, $k=10$ and batch 1,000.
Vogue uses 4,096 IVF lists; the other three use 8,192.
Vogue observes probes 16/\allowbreak{}32/\allowbreak{}64/\allowbreak{}96/\allowbreak{}128/\allowbreak{}192/\allowbreak{}256/\allowbreak{}384/\allowbreak{}512 and
$\alpha\in\{16,32,64,128\}$ over 27 tuples. ArXiv adds probe 1,024
and uses $\alpha\in\{25,50,100,200\}$ over 29 tuples.
Both OpenAI grids use probes 32/\allowbreak{}64/\allowbreak{}128/\allowbreak{}256/\allowbreak{}512/\allowbreak{}1,024;
their observed multipliers are respectively
$\{4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512\}$ and
$\{2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256\}$, over 37 and 39 tuples.
The reported scheduled path uses four groups on Vogue and one block
elsewhere. OpenAI uses TF32 rotation/centroid GEMMs in historical v69;
the v72 FP32 sensitivity is a separate family (\cref{sec:7-precision}).

\paragraph{CAGRA fp32 and int8.}
Each representation has 64 points per dataset: graph degrees 32/\allowbreak{}64,
intermediate degree 128, \texttt{ivf\_pq} construction,
\texttt{itopk\_size} in 32/\allowbreak{}64/\allowbreak{}96/\allowbreak{}128/\allowbreak{}192/\allowbreak{}256/\allowbreak{}384/\allowbreak{}512 and search width
1/\allowbreak{}2/\allowbreak{}4/\allowbreak{}8. Int8 records quantile 0.99 for dataset scaling and includes
query quantisation in the host search boundary.

\paragraph{IVF-PQ.}
Eight-bit subcodes use 192/\allowbreak{}384/\allowbreak{}768-byte codes at dimension 768,
and 384/\allowbreak{}768/\allowbreak{}1,536-byte codes on OpenAI. Each length has fp16/fp32
lookup tables and probes 16/\allowbreak{}32/\allowbreak{}64/\allowbreak{}96/\allowbreak{}128/\allowbreak{}192/\allowbreak{}256/\allowbreak{}384/\allowbreak{}512:
54 points per dataset. Refinement ratio is one; list counts match JHQ, while code lengths/memory differ.

\paragraph{IVF-RaBitQ and brute force.}
RaBitQ uses 4/8/9 bits, probes 16/\allowbreak{}32/\allowbreak{}64/\allowbreak{}96/\allowbreak{}128/\allowbreak{}192/\allowbreak{}256/\allowbreak{}384/\allowbreak{}512/\allowbreak{}768/\allowbreak{}1,024 and modes LUT16/LUT32/QUANT4/QUANT8 (no LUT16 on OpenAI-3072). OpenAI adds 4,096-list indexes to the 8,192-list default; the registry records combinations. Each dataset has one FP32 squared-L2 brute-force point. Untested coverage is not a failure.

\paragraph{Auxiliary grids.}
LUT tests cover six datasets, probes 8/32/128/512, $\glut\in\{1,2,4,8\}$ and $\alpha=100$: 24 cells/96 arms. Budget tests use probes 128/\allowbreak{}512, $A=(200,100,64,32,16,8,4,2)$, 64 draws per $S\in\{32,64,128\}$ and $\epsilon=1$. FULL uses all 500 calibration queries. Held-out counts are 500 (Stella 499).  Boundaries are specified in
\cref{sec:a-budget-contract,sec:a-supplement}.

\par\endgroup

\section{Correctness and Numerical Evidence}
\label{sec:b-correctness}
\Cref{tab:b-checks} separates numerical, algorithmic and memory evidence.
Chapter 5 proves order for computed scores under explicit contracts; recall evaluates raw-vector recovery.

\par\medskip\noindent\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}
\centering\captionsetup{hypcap=false}
\captionof{table}[Validation coverage]{Validation coverage and the object actually checked.}
\label{tab:b-checks}
\footnotesize\setlength{\tabcolsep}{4pt}
\begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{@{}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{.22\linewidth}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}X@{}}
\toprule
Boundary & Completed evidence and scope \\
\midrule
Representation & Four all-row offset/ID audits; sampled raw-input FP64
recoding and stored-matrix geometry; TF32 deviations identified \\
Cartesian LUTs & Real-arithmetic factorisation; 96 timed arms; T4
per-candidate FP32 error and ranking diagnostics across four table forms \\
Global selection & T4: 270 configurations, 69,120 query instances;
55,296 grouped instances match strict CPU complete-key sorting in order \\
Shared bound & 48 paired checks; extracted scalar 64-bit PTX and toolkit
SASS support whole-key access; actual driver SASS not captured \\
Scheduling & 250 variant/configuration and 234,320 query comparisons,
retaining distinctions between ID sets and tie order \\
Probe selector & 1,792 synthetic cases with zero failures; real-query
ID/offset checks, relative to computed routing scores \\
Budget search & 2,304 monotone sampled curves and 12 FULL enumeration
matches; 18,432 sampled grid counts reproduce full-pool subset sums \\
