The smaller representation-audit databases have identical primary and
residual bytes across one-/two-pass builds when joined by ID.
Corrections differ by at most $8.94\times10^{-8}$ and 1/\allowbreak{}1/\allowbreak{}40 rows change
list assignment; Stella validates its natural two-pass path
(\cref{sec:4-representation-audit}). T4 supplies a strict computed-score reference (\cref{sec:a-t4-t5}). A controlled same-model cross-process Vogue diagnosis remains undone: matching archived probe/primary dumps accompany recall 0.9642/\allowbreak{}0.9644. Within-run checks do not explain this anomaly.

\section{Secondary Results and Evidence Status}
\label{sec:b-secondary}
\paragraph{Adverse regimes.}
Worst scheduling regret is 1.217 at batch 256; Vogue E1 ratios span 0.895--1.175 (\cref{sec:7-6}). T5 CAGRA fp32 wins all batch-8 datasets at 0.97; batch-32 near ties depend on the estimator (\cref{sec:7-smallbatch}).





